**Yara** (/' *jɑːraː* /, *[[intin|Intin]]*: やら) is the element of Air and the goddess of the Sky, Travel and Luck

-----

# Religion
House of Worship, Communion, Differences, Mythology

The Zanagi religion is different form a normal reliigon, instead of following a deity's commands and order, the Zanaki follow a way to live. This is specifically shown in their forms of meditation and self reflection.

A large part of the Zanagi[^zanagi] religion is the religious meditation. It is one of the core tenets of the Zanaki[^zanaki]. It basically entails an opening of the mind to the voices of the heavens, called the *Tenokoe*^[tenokoe]. The Zanagi religion promotes finding your own form of meditation, but advises secluded, open-air location for the greatest success. Along with the *Tenokoe*, self reflection is the second part of the Zanagi meditation. Here the importance of self is contrasted with the reflection of itself. You can only rely on yourself if you're trying to best your best self. It involves *Jibun Kaku*[^jk], writing letters to yourself.

Although the Zanagi religion is individual, it still has houses of worship in a similar manner to other religions. These are called Sanctums and are to promote ones ability and power of meditation. There a specific isolated areas surrounded by still pools for meditation specifically. As-well they are the location of the *Toppukaito*[^toppukaito] initiation rituals.

Yara is one of the lower scaled Elemental deities. She is not dominant as other deities can be. However she featured heavily in the ascension of Daglir, as she had previously been a twinned deity with Daglir's Predeccessor. They had combined in the domains of Travel storm and luck, and were for a long time worshiped in unison. Yet Daglir's Predeccessor was always the more popular. This came to light when she ascended to the Elemental domain of Water. She shifted to the forefront, while Yara remained behind.

Yet after Daglir's Predeccessor's passing and his ascension, Yara gained an influx of power. As many followers didn't transfer their divine worship to the new water deity, but to the familiar Yara. She gained ever more and ascended to the previously empty Elemental domain of Wind, and for the first time ever completing the Elemental domain.

## Sects
Different Sects/Cults
* Mae of **Sora**
The Mae of Sora are mainly followers of the Sky. They are zealous practitioners of *Toppukaito*[^toppukaito]. They mostly reside in more mountainous areas.
* Mae of **Toraberu**
The Toraberu are believers in the influence of wind on Travel. They are mostly innkeepers, stablemates or harbormasters, who deliver boons upon travelers. 
* Mae of **Arashi**
The Arashi believe in the power of storms and lightning. They worship secluded from the other Mae's and have for centuries researched how to harness the power of lighting.
* Mae of **Koun**
The Koun are the Mae of Luck, and how to influence it. They are casino-hands or swindlers who wish to use her powers to influence the power of luck. 
## Structure
### Venerated Ancestors
*See also: [[list-of-zanagi-venerated-ancestors|List of Zanagi Venerated Ancestors]]*
In the Zanagi[^zanagi] religion there some which succeed in such miraculous acts, that they are worshiped themselves. This may include miraculous or incredible words of wisdom. They are addressed by the *Tohu*[^tohu] prefix, which is given to them posthumously.

# Cultural
## Heavensward Fest
The Heavensward Fest is a communal celebration of the wisdom and power of the Zanaki[^zanaki]. It starts 5 days before, with the sending of spell kites. These arcane kites carry a basket of gifts to someone the sender admires in any way. During the summoning of a kite it is sent to a place where the sender has to have been before or know where it is. Days later the festivities pick up again. As communities of Zanaki celebrate the night of the year. Wine, beer and various liquors get passed around during the feast of the night. I

## Temple of the Skies
The Temple of the Skies is a legendary complex of temples, in its prime it had grown to the size of a city. There many magical inventions where created, as was recorded in many other records. Here is where the practice of *Toppukaito*[^toppukaito] originated and many other pioneering Elemental magics were created. Yet all of this knowledge was lost upon the destruction of this complex by a massive earthquake, splitting it in half. 
%%library of alexandria%%

## Toppukaito [^toppukaito]
*See also: Toppukaito*
*Toppukaito* is the art of flying for this without the boon of wings. It uses elemental magics along with a handcrafted glider. The elemental magics are learned during a ritual in a Sanctum, here they lean the spell to takeoff. This allows a user to create a gust of wind under them and their glider to reach a high altitude and glide upon the strong winds higher up. This has proven to be a effective method of transportation. The glider is handcrafted by its user. They use natures design of wings in their design. This being the only similarity of appearance in them, as some may look like bird wings and other like dragon wings.

